This Solidity code provides the `SimpleEtherWallet` contract with a `deposit` function that checks for non-zero deposits and a `withdraw` function that implements the Checks-Effects-Interactions pattern to prevent reentrancy attacks. The `withdraw` function first updates the state (effects) and then interacts with the recipient (interactions), ensuring that the recipient cannot re-enter the `withdraw` function before the state is updated (checks).

The `Attack` contract demonstrates a potential reentrancy attack by having a fallback function that calls `withdraw` when it receives Ether. When the `Attack` contract deposits Ether into the `SimpleEtherWallet`, it will be able to withdraw it before the state update in the `withdraw` function. This will result in the attacker being able to withdraw more Ether than they deposited, leading to a loss of funds.

